{"name":"Tiger Claw","hex":"#e1daca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Panthera tigris, a large predatory mammal of the cat family, indigenous to Asia.","A male tiger; as opposed to a tigress."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A final shouted phrase, accompanied by a jump or outstretched arms, at the end of a cheer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger"},{"term":"claw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A curved, pointed, horny projection on each digit of the foot of a mammal, reptile, or bird.","A foot equipped with such."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To scratch or to tear at.","To use the claws to seize, to grip."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claw"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erythrina variegata","blocks":[{"text":"Erythrina variegata, commonly known as tiger's claw or Indian coral tree, is a species of Erythrina native to the tropical and subtropical regions of eastern Africa, the Indian subcontinent, northern Australia, and the islands of the Indian Ocean and the western Pacific Ocean east to Fiji."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Indian_coral_tree_Munnar_Kerala_Erythrina_variegata.jpg/330px-Indian_coral_tree_Munnar_Kerala_Erythrina_variegata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrina_variegata"},{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg/330px-Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger"},{"title":"Claw","blocks":[{"text":"A claw is a curved, pointed appendage found at the end of a toe or finger in most amniotes. Some invertebrates such as beetles, spiders, and velvet worms have somewhat similar fine, hooked structures at the end of the leg or tarsus for gripping a surface as they walk. The pincers of crabs, lobsters, crayfish, shrimps, prawns and scorpions, more formally known as their chelae, are sometimes called claws."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cat_claw_closeup.jpg/330px-Cat_claw_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claw"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Flower_I_IMG_3974.jpg/500px-Flower_I_IMG_3974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Flower_I_IMG_3974.jpg/500px-Flower_I_IMG_3974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flower in Kolkata, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlower_I_IMG_3974.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Erythrina_variegata_Blanco1.217.png/120px-Erythrina_variegata_Blanco1.217.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Erythrina_variegata_Blanco1.217.png/250px-Erythrina_variegata_Blanco1.217.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Erythrina_variegata_Blanco1.217.png/120px-Erythrina_variegata_Blanco1.217.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","